s884:
According to subparagraphs "d", "f" and "h" of paragraph 1 of Article 674 of the Civil Code of Georgia, a waybill must contain the following details:
- d. the date and place where the goods are handed over, and the place of delivery;
- f. the usual name of the type of goods and the type of packaging, and for dangerous goods, their generally recognised designation;
- h. the weight of the goods or their quantity expressed in another way.

s888:
According to subparagraphs "a", "g" and "i" of paragraph 1 of Article 674 of the Civil Code of Georgia, a waybill must contain the following details:
- a. the date and place where it is issued;
- g. the quantity, marks and numbers of the goods being carried;
- i. the costs related to the carriage (the price of carriage, additional costs, import duties and other costs arising from the conclusion of the contract until delivery of the goods).

s894:
According to subparagraphs "a", "b" and "c" of paragraph 2 of Article 674 of the Civil Code of Georgia, where necessary, a waybill must contain additional details:
- a. a prohibition on transferring the goods to another vehicle;
- b. the costs that the consignor agrees to cover;
- c. the amount of any surcharge payable when the goods are sent.

s898:
According to subparagraphs "a", "b" and "c" of paragraph 2 of Article 674 of the Civil Code of Georgia, where necessary, a waybill must contain additional details:
- d. the value of the goods and a note of any special interest in their delivery;
- e. the consignor's instructions to the carrier on insuring the goods;
- g. a list of the documents handed to the carrier.

s913:
According to subparagraphs "a" and "b" of paragraph 1 of Article 676 of the Civil Code of Georgia, when accepting goods, the carrier must check:
- a. the number of items and whether the details in the waybill about their marks and numbers are correct;
- b. the external condition of the goods and their packaging.
